---
title: "Basic Fluid Mechanics - Hydraulics/Pneumatics"
code: "MEC-161"
category: "mechanical-engineering-technology"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Introduces theory, operation and maintenance of hydraulic/ pneumatics devices and systems. Emphasizes the properties of fluids, fluid flow, fluid statics, and the application of Bernoulli’s equation. Lecture 2 hours, Laboratory 2 hours, Total 4 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
